1581..1654 Comment "/// The winding number into the native integers, a fold that rests on the"
1655..1712 Comment "/// native model\'s laws. At `Loop(Unloop(x))` it computes"
1713..1784 Comment "/// `turn(unturn(native_wind(x)))`, which conversion does not reduce to"
1785..1861 Comment "/// `native_wind(x)` on a variable; the law `turnUnturn` states exactly that"
1862..1938 Comment "/// path, so `respects` names it for the first rule and `unturnTurn` for the"
1939..2013 Comment "/// second. The loop arms call the model\'s operations rather than spelling"
2014..2092 Comment "/// `n + 1`, so each side the rule relates is the law\'s own endpoint. The fold"
2093..2135 Comment "/// checks and owes what its two laws owe."
